+
+## 12. Active Managed / Scanner Click Path Proof
+
+`MANAGED-SCORE-PROOF-03` was added after the first click rerun showed `ScoreProof`,
+`EnginePathProof`, and `GPTPreview` but none of the click proof prefixes from
+`MANAGED-SCORE-PROOF-02`.
+
+### Rerun Finding
+
+The detail-chart open path was active, but the originally instrumented managed/scanner
+selection handlers were not proven to be the visible table click path. This means one
+of the following must be distinguished at runtime:
+
+- the visible table is not the same object as `self.tbl_ai_managed` or `self.tbl_market_all`;
+- click/selection is handled by a different Qt signal than the original handler;
+- the add button returns early before the previous add proof point;
+- center/detail refresh uses a detail-open path instead of the center refresh path.
+
+### ManagedScoreActiveSurfaceProof
+
+`ManagedScoreActiveSurfaceProof` is emitted at table build/refresh and records the
+actual visible table surface without changing the UI.
+
+Fields:
+
+- `event`: `surface_discovery_build`, `surface_discovery_refresh`, or `signal_connected`
+- `widget_role`: `managed` or `scanner`
+- `object_name`
+- `python_id`
+- `visible`
+- `enabled`
+- `row_count`
+- `col_count`
+- `headers`
+- `parent_class`
+- `table_attr_name`
+- `submitted=0`
+
+### Active Signal Proof
+
+The visible managed/scanner tables receive proof-only signal connections:
+
+- `cellClicked`
+- `cellDoubleClicked`
+- `currentCellChanged`
+- `itemSelectionChanged`
+- `selectionModel().currentChanged`
+- `selectionModel().selectionChanged`
+
+The existing UI handlers are not removed or replaced. The proof connections only emit
+`ManagedScoreClickProof` or `ScannerScoreClickProof` and include `table_python_id`.
+
+### Add Path Early Return Proof
+
+`ManagedPoolAddProof` now includes:
+
+- `event=before_add_request`
+- `event=already_exists`
+- `event=before_add`
+- `event=after_add`
+
+This proves whether the active add request reaches `_add_symbol_to_ai_pool`, whether
+it exits early because the symbol already exists, and whether scanner score and managed
+score remain separate after add. No scanner score copy logic was added.
+
+### Center Detail Proof
+
+`CenterSelectionProof` is also emitted from the active detail-open path with
+`event=detail_open`. This records the selected symbol and score source before any
+existing GPT preview path is allowed to continue.
+
+### Safety Boundary
+
+This proof pass does not change:
+
+- managed score calculation;
+- scanner fallback calculation;
+- UI labels or columns;
+- provider/API connection logic;
+- Router, Execution, Order, or RiskGuard behavior;
+- database or runtime data schemas.
+
+`FUNCTION-FIX-03` remains the later fix candidate if the proof logs confirm a real
+SSOT collision between managed score and scanner display score.
+
+## MANAGED-SCORE-SSOT-01
+
+MANAGED-SCORE-SSOT-01 defines the AITS symbol score display owner as Basic/local
+calculation.
+
+- Left Managed Candidates, right AI Theme Scanner, and detail chart score displays
+  must use the same AITS score meaning.
+- GPT/GEMINI are not score calculators; they remain interpretation, judgement, or
+  briefing providers.
+- The Scanner display fallback must not be shown as a real score.
+- When a Scanner row can be evaluated with local market context, the UI displays the
+  Basic/local calculation score.
+- When a Scanner row cannot be evaluated, the UI shows a non-numeric state such as
+  `데이터부족` or `계산대기` instead of a fake numeric score.
+- Adding a Scanner symbol to Managed Pool must not copy the Scanner display score.
+  Managed rows continue through the managed/local calculation flow.
+- Score formula improvements are intentionally deferred to a later goal.
